-- --- Programme ↔ career mapping (215) -----------------------------------------------
--
-- **The rows §27 actually ranks programmes on.** A programme's RIASEC compatibility is the
-- *weighted average* of its linked careers' Holland codes (`programRiasecCompatibility`); a
-- programme with no mapping takes the neutral 50 and is indistinguishable from every other
-- unmapped one.
--
-- Written on the **canonical** programme (migration 0040): every college offering inherits it
-- through the `program_career_links` view, and `program_careers` is left empty for the
-- college-specific extras an admin adds later.
--
-- Each link is graded direct, related or conditional (migration 0041) — 64 direct, 113 related, 38 conditional.
-- The grading rule is written out above `MAPPINGS` in the generator. BROAD roles are **not**
-- linked at all: attaching transferable-skill roles to every programme would drag every
-- programme's average toward the same mean and flatten the ranking this catalog exists to
-- sharpen.

